  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Integrating high-throughput DSC, dilatometry, and third-generation CALPHAD will accurately and efficiently determine melting and liquid-phase thermodynamic properties across single-phase high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6382313::web::011::properties_of_neat_materials",
        "PMC7412006::web::014::2_7_calphad_modeling",
        "PMC8950179::web::007::3_1_the_third_generation_gibbs_energy_ex",
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "DSC can identify melting through an endothermic thermal signal.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6382313::web::011::properties_of_neat_materials",
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melting in the proposed high-entropy alloys will produce a sharp DSC peak.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dilatometry can measure the volume discontinuity at melting in these alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Third-generation CALPHAD can account jointly for thermal and configurational entropy contributions relevant to high-entropy-alloy melting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8950179::web::007::3_1_the_third_generation_gibbs_energy_ex",
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "An inert atmosphere prevents oxidation during the high-temperature measurements.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The DSC-peak onset and shape translate atomic-scale disorder and configurational entropy into measurable fusion enthalpy and entropy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6382313::web::011::properties_of_neat_materials",
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A discontinuity in thermal expansion at melting provides a measurable representation of the melting volume change.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7412006::web::014::2_7_calphad_modeling"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "DSC is sufficiently sensitive to detect small heat-capacity changes near melting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Configurational entropy can have a large influence on alloy entropy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fusion enthalpy can be derived by integrating the DSC melting signal.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6382313::web::011::properties_of_neat_materials",
        "PMC7513177::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fusion entropy can be calculated from fusion enthalpy and melting temperature.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.measurements",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6382313::web::011::properties_of_neat_materials"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Matching measured fusion enthalpy and entropy to CALPHAD predictions characterizes the alloy free-energy landscape.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7412006::web::014::2_7_calphad_modeling",
        "PMC8950179::web::007::3_1_the_third_generation_gibbs_energy_ex"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The combined experimental-computational framework reduces uncertainty relative to one-off measurements and separate CALPHAD assessments.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The integrated approach will determine fusion properties within approximately 5–10% of benchmark values.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The approach will enable systematic mapping and prediction across high-entropy-alloy composition space.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Traditional single-run DSC and independent CALPHAD assessments generally have larger uncertainties and lower efficiency for multicomponent alloys.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The approach is primarily applicable to compositionally homogeneous, single-phase disordered solid-solution high-entropy alloys.",
